From 101abee687f0f4004ce2348fb26f0cd7aa17568b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:36:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PRO: white balance in Kelvin, contrast, noise reduction,
 sharpening

The HAL offers MANUAL_POST_PROCESSING. White balance gains for a colour
temperature are computed the way a DNG reader does it: the point on the
Planckian locus, its XYZ, and the camera response through the colour
matrix interpolated in 1/T between the two calibration illuminants; the
camera to sRGB matrix stays the one the automatic white balance used last.
Contrast replaces the tone curve with the sRGB curve plus a monotonic S;
noise reduction and sharpening take the modes the camera lists.

In PRO video the PRO controls stay on screen while recording; the live
session applies them without reopening.

Signed-off-by: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
